     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the metformin maximum, so I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Labeled maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't raise that ceiling.\n- **Risk:** At 5,100 mg/day the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day). This is the maximum IR dose, and 1700 may be a typo for 850.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg PO two or three times daily**, if this is a new start with titration.\n\nIf you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose is intentional. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
